Qubit Office — asset licence and attribution
============================================

This file covers the office's bundled and user-built THEME ART only. Qubit's
source code is licensed under the MIT licence in LICENSE; nothing here changes
that licence.

Code vs art
-----------
* Qubit code, including the theme contract, the local theme builder, the
  extractor, the calibration tool, the sprite/card renderers and the shipped
  game bundle, is original Qubit material under the root LICENSE (MIT).
* The office art is not Qubit's to relicense. The art listed below remains the
  property of its author and is used under the terms stated for each pack.
* The art is sliced, positioned and composited by the local builder. It is not
  used to train models and it is not used to generate new art.

LimeZu — Modern Interiors, Modern User Interface, and the character/portrait art
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The owner purchased the LimeZu packs used to build local office themes. Credit
is required on every surface that ships the art:

    Office art: LimeZu — https://limezu.itch.io

The Modern Interiors licence permits editing and use in any commercial or
non-commercial project and requires credit to the artist. It forbids reselling
or redistributing the asset to others.

The Modern User Interface licence says the same, and additionally excludes NFT
minting:

    YOU CAN: edit and use the asset in any commercial or non commercial
    project, except NFT minting.
    YOU CAN'T: resell or distribute the asset to others; edit and resell the
    asset to others.
    Credits required.

Therefore:

* The repository ships the theme RECIPE (semantic tokens, part indices and
  template metadata), never the purchased atlases, the raw .zip packs, the
  extracted parts, or a derived atlas. Each person builds locally from their own
  purchase.
* No resale, redistribution, sublicensing or NFT minting of the art is allowed.
* The purchased Modern Interiors / Modern User Interface packs are governed by
  LimeZu's own paid-art commercial licence, **not** by a Creative Commons
  licence. That licence permits commercial use and requires credit, and it
  expressly forbids reselling or redistributing the assets. The recipe-only
  rule above is the practical consequence.

**CC-BY is not the licence of the purchased packs.** Describing them as CC-BY
would be wrong, because CC-BY permits redistribution and these licences forbid
it. CC-BY 4.0 applies only to Serene Village, below, and Serene Village is not
used by the Qubit Office v1 theme.

**Serene Village is the CC-BY exception (not used in v1).** Its separate CC-BY
4.0 terms require attribution and carry no source-sharing obligation (CC-BY,
not CC-BY-SA):

    Title:   Serene Village
    Author:  LimeZu
    Source:  https://limezu.itch.io
    Licence: CC-BY 4.0 — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
